WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.468
-You guys, Thanksgiving is
just three days away.

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:05.004
[ Cheers ]

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:07.107
I saw that tomorrow
President Trump will pardon

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:08.575
a turkey at the White House.

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:09.808
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:09.808 --> 00:00:11.578
Then he'll spend the next week
criticizing him

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.679
for not thanking him enough.

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:15.515
[ As Trump ] "I should've let
you got eaten."

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:19.318
[ Laughter ]

00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:21.120
[ Normal voice ] Actually, the
White House just posted photos

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.423
of the two turkeys Trump
will pardon,

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:25.391
and they also released photos
of the two turkeys

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:26.859
Trump refuses to pardon.
Take a look.

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:27.893
There they are, yeah.
-Wow.

00:00:27.893 --> 00:00:32.031
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:34.534
-A bit of a scandal.
A bit of a scandal.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:35.868
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:39.338
It came out that National
Security Advisor H.R. McMaster

00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:42.408
called President Trump an idiot,
and said he had the intelligence

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:43.409
of a kindergartner.

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:44.710
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:45.879
And Trump said,
[ As Trump ] "Oh, yeah?

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:47.613
Then why am I reading at
a first-grade level...

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:50.049
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:53.520
...and tweeting at
a sixth-grade level!"

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:54.654
[ Normal voice ] Calm down.

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:57.423
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:59.925
[ As Trump ] "I'm gonna go have
lunch with the turkeys."

00:00:59.925 --> 00:01:01.027
[ Normal voice ] What?

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.095
[ As Trump ] "Not only am
I pardoning them,

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.396
I'm hanging out
with them all week."

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.498
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:07.066
[ Normal voice ] This weekend,
Trump sent a tweet where

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:10.369
he criticized Senator Jeff Flake
for saying bad things about

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:11.871
quote, "your favorite
President."

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.272
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:15.074
People were like, "He said
bad things about Obama?"

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:16.509
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:20.313
He's talking about me --

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:22.147
Well, this is pretty big.
After saying that he'd let

00:01:22.147 --> 00:01:25.251
people import elephant trophies
into the U.S.,

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:28.788
Trump got a lot of backlash from
the public and changed his mind.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.656
Yeah, Trump's really --
He's really trying to win back

00:01:30.656 --> 00:01:33.092
animal lovers, even made his own
nature documentary

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:34.260
that's coming out.
-Oh.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.628
-Yeah, watch this.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:37.196
[ As Trump ]
This is Donald Trump,

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:38.598
and I love animals

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:41.534
which is why I made
Trump's Planet Earth.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:44.704
I'm gonna tell you about all my
favorite animals, such as --

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:47.006 line:0%
the chimichanga,

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:49.275 line:0%
the waaaalrus,

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.144 line:0%
Mitch McConnell,

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:52.645 line:0%
the topanga,

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:55.348 line:0%
Mufasa, and, of course,
my favorite,

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:58.083 line:0%
orange tan.

00:01:58.083 --> 00:01:59.084
[ Normal voice ]
It's weird, right?

00:01:59.084 --> 00:02:02.822
-Orange tan?
-Orange tan.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.724
-Wow.

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:07.493
-Meanwhile, Al Franken said
that he isn't resigning,

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:09.996
but will spend
the next few days reflecting.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.464
Reflecting is a political term
meaning, "hope someone else

00:02:12.464 --> 00:02:14.166
gets busted and this
whole thing blows over."

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:15.768
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.804
Smart.

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:20.473
Another big story here,
last night Charles Manson died

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.308
at the age of 83.

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:25.178
Which means today he met
his new roommates, Adolf, Osama,

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:27.046
and the Time Warner
customer service reps.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:32.352
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:34.787
That's right,
Charles Manson passed away.

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:37.189
Then "Dancing with the Stars"
was like, "Well, on to O.J.

00:02:37.189 --> 00:02:39.625
All right here we go.
We gotta -- make some calls.

00:02:39.625 --> 00:02:42.461
Get on that."

00:02:42.461 --> 00:02:44.096
This is cool.
Last night, the balloons

00:02:44.096 --> 00:02:46.332
for the Macy's Thanksgiving Day
Parade were inflated.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:47.600
It's a big deal.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.436
This year is actually the
parade's 91st anniversary.

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.005
Isn't that wild?
That's amazing, yeah.

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:54.340
[ Applause ]

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.509
I think you can sort of tell
the balloons are getting

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:58.378
a little older though.
I'll show you what I mean.

00:02:58.378 --> 00:03:01.047
For example, here's what
the Elf on the Shelf balloon

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:02.348
used to look like.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:03.849
Here's what it looks like now.

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:06.318
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:06.318 --> 00:03:08.320
-Wow.
-Yeah, I mean --

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:10.623
Here's what the Charlie Brown
balloon used to look like.

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.258
Here's what it looks like now.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:13.325
You see what I'm saying?
-Wow.

00:03:13.325 --> 00:03:16.095
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:18.164
-And finally, here's what
the Ronald McDonald

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:19.165
used to look like.

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.966
Here's what it looks like now.

00:03:20.966 --> 00:03:22.301
-Wow.
-And it's just very, very --

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:24.436
They might want to work on
the balloons a little bit.

00:03:24.436 --> 00:03:26.572
We'll be there.

00:03:26.572 --> 00:03:29.041
That's right,
this Thursday is Thanksgiving.

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:32.278
It's going to be Donald Trump's
first Thanksgiving as President.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:33.446
A lot of people are wondering

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.147
what a Trump family
Thanksgiving is like.

00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:36.749
Well, we have an expert
on the topic.

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:39.285 line:0%
Please welcome "Tonight Show"
correspondent Patty Harrison.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:40.553 line:0%
Hey, Patty.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:44.324 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:44.324 --> 00:03:46.793 line:0%
-Thanks, Jimmy, it's really
great to be back.

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:47.993
-Patty, what can you tell us

00:03:47.993 --> 00:03:49.862
about the Trumps'
Thanksgiving plans?

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:52.364
-I'm actually a long-time friend
of the family,

00:03:52.364 --> 00:03:54.700
so I eat with them every year.
-Really?

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.869
You spend Thanksgiving
with the Trumps?

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:59.471
-Yeah. A few years ago, I told
them I'm Eric Trump's wife,

00:03:59.471 --> 00:04:00.907
and no one questioned it.

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:02.174
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.174 --> 00:04:03.476
-Makes sense.
Okay --

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:06.178
How does a typical Trump family
Thanksgiving work?

00:04:06.178 --> 00:04:08.514
-First, let's talk
seating arrangements.

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:12.050
I sit at the big table
with Donald, Melania, Ivanka,

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:13.686
and Jared.
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:17.156
-Eric and Don Jr. sit
at the kids' table.

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:19.392
-Oh, perfect, yep.
-And Tiffany sits outside.

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:21.561
[ Audience ohs ]
-Okay -- Now,

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:24.196
do you guys say grace?
-Absolutely, Jimmy.

00:04:24.196 --> 00:04:26.665
The Trumps are a family driven
by values.

00:04:26.665 --> 00:04:29.401
We all hold hands and read
from the good book,

00:04:29.401 --> 00:04:30.703
"The Art of the Deal."

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.070
-Okay, yeah.

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:34.040
And then what happens?

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:37.109
-They bring out the turkey,
and it's a free-for-all.

00:04:37.109 --> 00:04:40.280
Eric grabs a wing,
Ivanka grabs a thigh,

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:42.048
Donald Trump grabs
a turkey by the --

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:44.383
-All right, all right.
Okay, Patty, Patty, Patty.

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:46.085
Wait a second.

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:49.087
What about dessert, do they have
apple pie or pumpkin pie?

00:04:49.087 --> 00:04:51.357
-Actually, for dessert,
we have créme brulée,

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:53.726
which Melania flambés
just by staring at it

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:55.695
with her fiery gaze
of steely regret.

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:59.365
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:02.602
-Wow, and how does
the night end?

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:04.070
-It's beautiful.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:08.641
Trump, Don Jr., and Eric all sit
on the couch watching football.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:11.210
And if you squint hard enough,
they start to look like

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.445
the colors of
the changing leaves.

00:05:13.445 --> 00:05:14.514
-Oh, that's beautiful.

00:05:14.514 --> 00:05:17.349
Thank you.
Patty Harrison, everybody.

00:05:17.349 --> 00:05:18.351
Thank you, Patty.

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:24.156
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.156 --> 00:05:27.693
Hey, I saw that the Georgia Dome
was demolished today in Atlanta.

00:05:27.693 --> 00:05:28.927
Did you see this?

00:05:28.927 --> 00:05:30.363
It's fantastic.

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:32.465
A cameraman
for the weather channel

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:34.367
had a perfect shot lined up,
because they we're going

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:36.502
to demolish the Georgia Dome,
yeah.

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:39.404
So he's got it all lined up,
perfect shot, and then he ran

00:05:39.404 --> 00:05:40.906
into a little trouble.

00:05:40.906 --> 00:05:42.408
Take a look at this.

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:43.876
[ Crashing ]

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:44.911
There he goes.

00:05:47.547 --> 00:05:57.590 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:02.361
[ Applause ]

00:06:02.361 --> 00:06:04.864
Meanwhile, everyone on the bus
was like, "Wow, what a view!

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:06.198
When are you going to see
something like this?

00:06:06.198 --> 00:06:09.001
It's award winning."

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:11.036
Some news out of England.
I saw that Queen Elizabeth

00:06:11.036 --> 00:06:12.571
and Prince Philip are
celebrating

00:06:12.571 --> 00:06:16.709
their 70 anniversary by getting
new portraits together.

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:18.477
It was a big day for them
and a huge day

00:06:18.477 --> 00:06:20.245
for the photographer at Sears.

00:06:20.245 --> 00:06:22.247
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:22.247 --> 00:06:24.350
Cock your head like that.

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:27.353
This is going viral, at a high
school wrestling match in Texas.

00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:29.121
A referee used a
pretty interesting move

00:06:29.121 --> 00:06:31.056
to get in position.
Take a look at this.

00:06:31.056 --> 00:06:37.230
[ Crowd noise ]

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:42.168
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.168 --> 00:06:44.069
Come on.
-Come on.

00:06:44.069 --> 00:06:46.972
Come on.
-What, that's it?

00:06:46.972 --> 00:06:49.174
Come on.

00:06:49.174 --> 00:06:52.611
Can we see that again?
I just want to see --

00:06:52.611 --> 00:06:54.213
-It's not about me, man.
It's about the kids.

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:56.682
-Even crazier,
he walked home like that.

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:58.150
-Are you serious?

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:01.320
-I think it might be time
to start drug testing the refs.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.655
I really do.

00:07:03.655 --> 00:07:05.391
And finally, I read that
for the first time,

00:07:05.391 --> 00:07:07.526
you're going to need a
reservation to visit Santa

00:07:07.526 --> 00:07:09.695
at Macy's.

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:11.063
But if you don't mind the smell
of whiskey,

00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:14.266
there's still a zero wait
to visit Santa at JC Penney.

00:07:14.266 --> 00:07:16.202
We have a great show tonight.
Give it up for The Roots!

